Thankyou! I managed to get the run the simulation all the different scenarios, but I also want each scenario (of the 45) to run 10 times. Previously I used this code in order to do so:

env <- lapply(1:10, function(i) {

simmer("truck consolidation") %>%

    add_resource("loadingdocks",1)%>%

    add_resource("unloadingdocks",1)%>%

    add_resource("truck",9999)%>%

    add_generator(name = "order" ,

                  trajectory = orders,

                  distribution = function() rexp(1,lambda),

                  mon = 2) %>%

    run(57600) %>%

    wrap()

})

But now that gives the following error when running envs %>% get_mon_arrivals():

Error in (function (x)  : unused argument (<environment>)

I have also tried this:

simulate<-function(param){

env <- lapply(1:param[["n_runs"]], function(i) {……}

.

. }

cases <- expand.grid(batchsize = c(1, 6, 10),

                     distance = c(50, 100, 500),

                     arrivalrate = c(2.4, 2.8, 3.2),

                     n_runs = 10)

system.time({

  envs <- parallel::mclapply(split(cases, 1:nrow(cases)), simulate,

